A||N||4||TheFiero64||Another ? for fiberglass guys out there? ||||5||
Z||000000||TheFiero64||11-21-2000||04:52 PM||||I just got the Mustang hood scoop for my decklid. I wand to put honeycomb mesh in the opening for looks and so no leaves get it. Is this possible and how? Here is a pic of the scoop and the screen. Please help me. Thanks in advance <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scoop_3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scoop2_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-21-2000||08:14 PM||||glue some little brackets to the deck lid and scoop. attach the screen to them. Epoxy should work to glue the brackets to the scoop. I'm not sure what will stick to the deck lid. You could do it with 3 L brackets on just the scoop. Depends how stiff the screen is how much anchorage it needs.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||11-21-2000||09:54 PM||||Here's what I did with the side scoops I made. Fill the spears with marglass body filler, and put a few lumps allong the top edge as well. Scuff the fiberglass with 36 grit so the marglass sticks well. Pre-drill 1/16" holes in the hardened marglass and use some small sheet metal screws 1/4" long to hold the screen in place. Also a good idea to put some edge trim (door edge guard) on the screen where it rests against the hood to keep it from rubbing through the paint, and it will also stiffen it up a bit.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-22-2000||06:28 AM||||if you have a large RV dealer in town (Winebego, Fleetwood etc) there service dept or part department has cauking tubes of this stuff called "Gorilla" or "Green" Snot......really.....I swear. You just spread a layer inside the glass part and press the screen on it, then wipe some more over the edges. They use it to assemble things like hood and compartment hinges to the fiberglass panels. Find one and open the front hood and youll see what Im talking about.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||11-22-2000||11:38 AM||||Thanks for the tips everyone. I will let you know how it comes out and what method I used.||||reg||7
